    "title": {
      "en": "Marsh Tit or Willow Tit?"
    },
    "text": {
      "en": "Voice first. A Marsh Tit calls an explosive “pitchou!”, a Willow Tit a nasal, buzzing “tchay-tchay”. Then the cap: glossy and neat for the Marsh Tit, dull and sooty for the Willow Tit. A Willow Tit has a larger, untidy bib and a pale wing panel. The habitat helps: Marsh Tit in dry deciduous woods, Willow Tit in damp woods."
    }
